WEBVTT

00:00.634 --> 00:02.514
- [Voiceover] Farmer Jan
is a vegetable farmer

00:02.514 --> 00:04.998
who divides his field
between broccoli crops

00:04.998 --> 00:06.531
and spinach crops.

00:06.531 --> 00:10.083
Last year, he grew six
tons of broccoli per acre,

00:10.083 --> 00:12.869
so six tons of broccoli per acre,

00:12.869 --> 00:15.748
and nine tons of spinach,

00:15.748 --> 00:17.931
nine tons of spinach per acre,

00:17.931 --> 00:21.414
for a total of 93 tons of vegetables.

00:21.414 --> 00:24.966
This year, he grew two
tons of broccoli per acre,

00:24.966 --> 00:29.169
so this year, he grew two
tons of broccoli per acre,

00:29.169 --> 00:32.559
and three tons of spinach per acre,

00:32.559 --> 00:35.229
and three tons of spinach per acre,

00:35.229 --> 00:38.458
for a total of 31 tons of vegetables.

00:38.458 --> 00:41.800
How many acres of broccoli
crops and how many acres

00:41.800 --> 00:45.028
of spinach crops does Farmer Jan have?

00:45.028 --> 00:46.467
So let's think about this.

00:46.467 --> 00:51.042
So let's say that the number
of acres of broccoli crops,

00:51.042 --> 00:54.385
let's call that B,

00:54.385 --> 00:57.589
and let's say the acres of spinach crops,

00:57.589 --> 01:01.537
acres of spinach crops, let's call that S.

01:01.537 --> 01:04.811
So how much broccoli is he going to grow

01:04.811 --> 01:07.388
in, I guess you could say, last year?

01:07.388 --> 01:09.385
Last year, how much broccoli did he grow?

01:09.385 --> 01:11.576
And let me just write this
down. This is last year.

01:11.576 --> 01:15.019
Last year.

01:15.019 --> 01:19.241
And they tell us, last
year he grew six tons

01:19.241 --> 01:21.453
of broccoli per acre.

01:21.453 --> 01:23.914
So if he grew six tons
of broccoli per acre,

01:23.914 --> 01:25.935
and he has B acres,

01:25.935 --> 01:29.860
well, that means he grew six tons per acre

01:29.860 --> 01:31.903
times B acres.

01:31.903 --> 01:36.499
So he grew 6B tons of broccoli last year.

01:36.499 --> 01:40.262
And by the same logic,
he grew how much spinach?

01:40.262 --> 01:45.022
Well, nine tons of spinach
per acre times S acres.

01:45.022 --> 01:49.311
So 9S tons of spinach,

01:49.311 --> 01:51.957
and then the total is 93 tons,

01:51.957 --> 01:55.534
so for a total of 93 tons of vegetables.

01:55.534 --> 01:59.132
So this is going to be equal to 93.

01:59.132 --> 02:01.315
So now let's think about this year.

02:01.315 --> 02:03.892
And in general, when you
tackle these, just think about,

02:03.892 --> 02:05.889
well, set the variables in general

02:05.889 --> 02:07.405
to what they're asking for, and then,

02:07.405 --> 02:10.181
how can you use the information
that they're giving us?

02:10.181 --> 02:13.477
So this year, how much
broccoli would he have grown?

02:13.477 --> 02:16.542
Well, he grew two tons
of broccoli per acre,

02:16.542 --> 02:19.701
so he grew two tons per acre.

02:19.701 --> 02:22.673
He has the same number of
acres. We can assume that.

02:22.673 --> 02:24.785
So two tons per acre times B acres

02:24.785 --> 02:28.106
is gonna be 2B tons of broccoli.

02:28.106 --> 02:30.242
And by that same logic, it's going to be,

02:30.242 --> 02:32.610
he grew three tons of spinach per acre.

02:32.610 --> 02:34.283
Well, he has S acres.

02:34.283 --> 02:36.651
Each of those acres,
he's growing three tons

02:36.651 --> 02:41.017
of spinach per acre, so it's
going to be 3S tons of spinach.

02:41.017 --> 02:42.827
And they tell us what that total is.

02:42.827 --> 02:47.395
That total is, for a total
of 31 tons of vegetables.

02:47.395 --> 02:50.112
So this is going to be equal to 31.

02:50.112 --> 02:52.456
And so now we have a
system of two equations

02:52.456 --> 02:56.962
with two unknowns, that we
can use to solve for B and S.

02:56.962 --> 03:00.026
So let's see. What do we
wanna solve for first?

03:00.026 --> 03:03.787
Well, what we could do, let
me rewrite the top equation.

03:03.787 --> 03:07.028
So we have 6B plus,

03:07.868 --> 03:12.261
plus 9S is equal to 93,

03:13.211 --> 03:15.321
is equal to 93.

03:15.321 --> 03:16.299
And the second equation,

03:16.299 --> 03:20.084
we'll let's try to eliminate the Bs.

03:20.084 --> 03:24.326
So let's multiply the second
equation by negative three.

03:24.326 --> 03:27.791
I'm gonna multiply the left
hand side by negative three,

03:27.791 --> 03:30.253
and I'm gonna multiply the right hand side

03:30.253 --> 03:31.623
by negative three.

03:31.623 --> 03:34.014
What am I going to get?

03:34.014 --> 03:37.335
Negative three times 2B is negative 6B.

03:37.335 --> 03:38.914
That was the whole point by multiplying it

03:38.914 --> 03:40.585
by negative three.

03:40.585 --> 03:44.685
Negative three times 3S is negative 9S,

03:44.685 --> 03:46.242
negative 9S.

03:46.242 --> 03:51.140
And then, negative three times 31 is going

03:51.140 --> 03:54.159
to be negative 93.

03:54.159 --> 03:57.688
So what do we get if we
now add the two sides

03:57.688 --> 03:59.477
of these equations?

03:59.477 --> 04:02.612
So on the left hand side,
6B minus 6B, that's zero.

04:02.612 --> 04:06.117
9S minus 9S, that's zero.
We're gonna get just zero.

04:06.117 --> 04:10.296
On the right hand side we get 93 minus 93.

04:10.296 --> 04:13.454
Well, that's still just going to be zero.

04:13.454 --> 04:16.356
So we have this situation
where we get zero equals zero,

04:16.356 --> 04:19.421
which is going to be true
no matter what X and Y are,

04:19.421 --> 04:22.092
and so this is a system
with an infinite number

04:22.092 --> 04:23.253
of solutions.

04:23.253 --> 04:26.482
So this has infinite,

04:27.592 --> 04:31.655
infinite number of solutions.

04:31.655 --> 04:33.491
So one way we could think about it is,

04:33.491 --> 04:34.861
these two constraints,

04:34.861 --> 04:37.460
they're not giving us enough information.

04:37.460 --> 04:40.317
There's an infinite number
of B and S combinations

04:40.317 --> 04:42.987
that would satisfy these equations,

04:42.987 --> 04:45.565
so they're not giving
us enough information

04:45.565 --> 04:50.325
to say exactly what B and S are.

04:50.325 --> 04:53.617
So there is not enough,

04:53.617 --> 04:56.495
not enough info!

04:56.495 --> 04:58.492
Put an exclamation mark there.
